+# Carry-Forward Inventory
+
+## Core idea
+
+A clean editorial inventory board turns an uncertain career transition into a visible set of portable assets. Four color-coded drawers—capabilities, values, relationships, and perspective—open one at a time, then lock together into a single carry-forward case.
+
+## Visual arc
+
+1. Begin with an empty luggage-tag question: “What deserves to come with you?”
+2. Establish the inventory as a deliberate filter, not a nostalgic scrapbook.
+3. Build four distinct inventory drawers with a focused question in each.
+4. Review all four categories as one organized system.
+5. Close by transforming the filled inventory into a forward-pointing case: the learner is not starting from zero.
+
+## Direction
+
+Use crisp paper-white cards on deep navy, restrained gold and blue accents, large type, and simple object motion. The inventory should feel practical, mature, and confidence-building. Motion is finite and purposeful: tags attach, drawers slide, check marks resolve, and the final case moves forward.
+
